# Document fixtures are compared byte for byte by the extraction tests, so no
# platform may rewrite their line endings. Git auto-detects the real PDFs as
# binary today, but corrupt.pdf is ASCII by design and git already announced it
# would convert LF to CRLF on the next checkout. Pin all of them rather than
# rely on heuristics: a mangled fixture fails as "the parser is broken", which
# is the most expensive kind of wrong.
test/fixtures/documents/** binary
